# pyro_emitfromflame

- Label: Pyro Emit from Flame
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 8
- Parameters: 122 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/pyro_emitfromflame.html
- Summary (EN): Burns up the flame field. Dissipates the flame over time and emits smoke (density) and temperature from the burned flame; can also add divergence to drive expansion in the simulation. Available since Houdini 22.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Pyro Emit from Flame consume le champ de flamme et en tire de la fumée, de la chaleur et, si besoin, de la divergence pour faire gonfler la simulation.

- Inputs meaning: ["flame: Float VDB representing the flame", "density: Float VDB that emitted smoke is combined with", "temperature: Float VDB that emitted heat is combined with", "divergence: Float VDB that flame expansion is combined with", "control_cooling (optional): control field for flame cooling", "control_density (optional): control field for density emission", "control_temperature (optional): control field for temperature emission", "control_divergence (optional): control field for flame expansion"]

- Key parameters: ["Activation: enables the node; runs only when the value is 1", "Cool Flame: when on, emitted amounts scale by how much flame was dissipated", "Dissipation Mode, Dissipation Rate, Subtraction Rate, Lifespan, Half-Life: flame decay controls", "Goal Value and Goal Tolerance: value the flame cools toward (usually zero), snapped there once close enough", "Emit Density / Emit Temperature / Enable Expansion: on or off switches for each output", "Operation: how emitted values combine with the incoming field (Add, Maximum, Average, Blend, Pull)", "Emission Scale (or Expansion Scale): output amount multiplier", "Flame Range and Emission Range: select the part of the flame field that emits, optionally remapped", "Acceleration, Deceleration, Blend: strength of push toward or mix with the incoming field (Pull and Blend)", "Use Ramp and Flame Ramp: shape the mapping from flame values to output", "Control Mask subsections (per section): Use Control Field, Control Range, Use Ramp, Control Ramp for spatial scaling"]

- Caveats: ["Requires DOP-level permissions; not in Houdini Core, only in Houdini FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education", "The Blend description under Expansion contains a typo on the page, so that wording may be imprecise"]

